WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.873
This video is sponsored by KiwiCo.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.340
Hello the internet, I am Gav.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.740
In this video, we're gonna
be recreating a viral TikTok

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.480
that a lot of you have very
kindly sent me, I thank you,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.700
of an Apple being levitated
on a jet of compressed air.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.140
Due to a phenomenon
called the Coanda effect,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.130
it should just stay exactly
in place on the compressed air

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.840
until eventually it goes
a little bit too fast

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.410
for itself and pops.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.150
Sounds like an excellent
subject for the Phantom.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.900
So why don't we give it a go?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.020
There certainly seems to
be some technique to it.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.310
This is 150 PSI compressor

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.980
but it seems to be less about the power

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.370
and more about the slow
build to keep it stable

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.180
'cause if I end up just flooring it,

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.440
it bounces up and down
like this and loses speed.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.240
It's all about sort of
getting it right on the edge

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.360
and then you can hear it revving up.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.050
It's actually, the sound
is the only indication

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.570
I have that I know I'm doing it right.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.030
And then eventually the
sound goes high enough

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.720
and you just got to clench
and hope for the best.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.800
So this apple is able to
perfectly defy gravity.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.320
As the jet of air bounces
off one side of the apple,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.420
it creates an area of low pressure

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.740
between the air and the curved surface.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.320
This area of low pressure
effectively pulls in the airflow

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.460
allowing it to follow
the curve of the apple.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.630
At this point, as the
curve surface of the apple

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.410
is putting a force on the air,

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.740
the air exerts an equal and opposite force

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.940
upward on the apple

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.590
and that's why it's able to
perfectly float in place.

00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:35.260
Whoa, this effect only works on objects

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.380
with a curved surface.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.900
So if this was a mutated cube apple,

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.550
it wouldn't work at all.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.040
It's pretty crazy, to my
eye when I'm looking at it,

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.820
I'm just looking at a blur

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.320
and then like one frame of
my eyes later, it's gone.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.130
It's like someone's just edited out

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.850
a moment of my life there.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.248
It's so fast.

00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:56.893
Bloody hell, look at
the RPM on that thing.

00:02:31.553 --> 00:02:33.423
That is baking.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.760
Well this camera's not fast enough.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.633
That is rapid.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.833
It's moving fast in slow motion.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.263
I need to cool Alabama.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.510
All right, it's been a few days

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.610
and Destin has come
through with this 2511.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.150
We now have access to 28,000
frames a second at 720p

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.530
which should be a lot better
for seeing the rotation

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:02.510
and potentially seeing
where the crack starts.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.830
Make sure you subscribe
to Smarter Everyday

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.450
because he's always helping me out.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.680
Just gonna do a bit of
apple art on some of these

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.913
so we can better track the rotation.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:25.600
Damn it.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.983
Awe, it's amazing, wow.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.610
You can actually see the skin of the apple

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.290
ripping in this, at this speed.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.850
That one gave me a rollicking on the hand.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:45.840
If I wasn't wearing gloves,

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.133
that one would really hurt I think.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.330
Okay, so now we can
roughly estimate how fast

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.320
the apple was spinning by
timing how long it takes

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.830
for this line to come
back around to the arrow.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.730
This was the final rotation of the apple

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.310
and based on the sound it was making

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.100
and the fact that it exploded,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.730
I'm gonna assume this was
the fastest rotation as well.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.580
One full rotation in 9.1 milliseconds.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.410
That's 109 rotations per second,

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.870
which reveals the apples nope speed

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.973
to be 6565 RPM.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.990
That was something, that was very sweaty,

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.270
very loud and slightly terrifying work

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.920
but I do think we've got some
lovely looking footage there

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.780
especially with the 2511.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.290
We saw a lot more that we didn't see

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.860
at 1000 frames a second,
like the skin ripping

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.400
almost as though the inside
of the apple has already split

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.900
And the skin is just the
final thing to give away.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.380
Absolutely mental and I
think I do now have to invest

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:47.400
